      "id": "uctk0rd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.1 Forts of Rajasthan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "UNESCO World Heritage Site (2013): The 'Hill Forts of Rajasthan' – Six forts were inscribed:",
      "id": "p07qiyj"
    },
    {
      "id": "tnhe40o",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Chittorgarh Fort – Largest fort in India by area (691 acres); Chittorgarh district",
        "Mehrangarh Fort – Jodhpur; built by Rao Jodha in 1459",
        "Kumbhalgarh Fort – Rajsamand; built by Rana Kumbha; second longest wall in world (36 km)",
        "Amber Fort – Jaipur; built by Raja Man Singh I",
        "Ranthambore Fort – Sawai Madhopur; earliest known fort of Rajasthan",
        "Gagron Fort – Jhalawar; a water fort (water on three sides)",
        "Jaisalmer Fort (Sonar Quila) – Jaisalmer; only living fort in India"
      ]
    },
